\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Nexus request flow. Routing (blue, lower path) depends only on the query embedding and the tool registry, never on the deep context, so it is depth-independent. KV-cache acceleration (upper, dashed) is a separate concern: an anchored splice is output-exact for $n_{\mathrm  {past}}\le 256$, while beyond it the depth-adaptive repair $R(n_{\mathrm  {past}})$ of \eqref  {eq:adaptive} escalates to a full re-prefill. Arguments are generated over a compressed textual signature, not over spliced KV.}}{5}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:arch}{{2}{5}{Nexus request flow. Routing (blue, lower path) depends only on the query embedding and the tool registry, never on the deep context, so it is depth-independent. KV-cache acceleration (upper, dashed) is a separate concern: an anchored splice is output-exact for $n_{\mathrm {past}}\le 256$, while beyond it the depth-adaptive repair $R(n_{\mathrm {past}})$ of \eqref {eq:adaptive} escalates to a full re-prefill. Arguments are generated over a compressed textual signature, not over spliced KV}{figure.2}{}}
