\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Physical splice with memory mapping. The compiled block is mapped via zero-copy \texttt  {\relax \fontsize  {9}{10pt}\selectfont  mmap} into virtual memory. Contiguous F16 keys and values are then blitted into the live cache; the trailing suffix fraction $R(n_{\mathrm  {past}})$ is re-decoded to stitch the seam. Layouts are transposed for soft-capped architectures (\S  \ref {sec:vtrans}).}}{5}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:atb}{{3}{5}{Physical splice with memory mapping. The compiled block is mapped via zero-copy \code {mmap} into virtual memory. Contiguous F16 keys and values are then blitted into the live cache; the trailing suffix fraction $R(n_{\mathrm {past}})$ is re-decoded to stitch the seam. Layouts are transposed for soft-capped architectures (\S \ref {sec:vtrans})}{figure.3}{}}
